-- `cargo xtask legacy-import --check` regenerates into a temporary directory and
-- diffs, so a hand edit here is a build failure rather than a surviving change.
-- The procedure these files implement is docs/data-migration.md.

-- The rollup archive: ~294 days of daily and hourly buckets with no raw behind
-- them, imported as pre-computed rows.
--
-- WHY THESE ARE PLAIN TABLES AND NOT PRE-SEEDED CONTINUOUS AGGREGATES
--
-- Rows inserted into a continuous aggregate on TimescaleDB 2.31 are accepted — the
-- INSERT is rewritten to the materialisation hypertable — and then destroyed by any
-- of three ordinary operations, none of which looks destructive:
--
--   * `CALL refresh_continuous_aggregate(level, lo, hi)` over the range. Measured:
--     21 of 29 pre-seeded buckets deleted, no error, no warning.
--   * the level's own scheduled refresh policy, once retention has dropped the raw
--     underneath. Measured: 41 of 83 buckets deleted by one policy run, and the
--     range destroyed was exactly the range whose raw had gone.
--   * adding a metric, which drops and recreates every level carrying it (D-15).
--     The chunk goes with the view.
--
-- A plain table survives all three, says in its own name that its rows were not
-- computed from raw, and costs 4 MB. docs/data-migration.md 3 and 5.

-- ------------------------------------------------------------------
-- observations_1d_legacy: 627 aggregate columns, 451 of which the Go views
-- computed. The other 176 land NULL, which is correct: the old system never
-- had that number, and a NULL says so where a zero would lie.
-- ------------------------------------------------------------------

